    {
      "name": "method",
      "caption": "The workflow uses one gait window and the same hidden targets for three predictors. The cross-leg benefit compares both-leg correction with own-leg correction. The movement score comes directly from observed-gait descriptors. The cross-leg score measures how unusual the prediction benefit is relative to normal reference data; the combined score is their fixed average. A token contains one joint across four frames. An anatomical lower-leg group contains knee, ankle, heel and toe points on one side over a short time span. The diagram motivates measurements, not a claim to recover neurological causes.",
      "inputs": {
        "docs/draft03/study_evidence.json": "7f24c996d16b4eb724e6a1a8590ab56c3a8e462165252cedf6b7fc392a7c17cf",
