    {
      "name": "normal_prediction",
      "caption": "All 28 held-out normal GAVD recording sources contribute. Each bar averages errors over the same hierarchy of targets, windows, sequences and recording sources; eight lower-leg joints receive equal weight. Scattered hiding removes individual tokens across the sequence. Grouped hiding scores nearby knee, ankle, heel and toe points hidden together on one side. The two panels test different missing-observation patterns, so their absolute errors should not be treated as a controlled comparison of training masks. Units are squared torso-scaled image coordinates.",
