      "name": "timing_limits",
      "caption": "The experiment substitutes permitted other-leg samples from four frames earlier or later, preserving the original target and body reference. Four frames correspond to about 0.27 seconds at 15 Hz. The left panel compares the two corrections on the common unshifted observations available for each shift: both-leg prediction is worse before either perturbation. The right panel shows the change after shifting, with conditional 95% intervals. All values are unchanged; 27 held-out normal recordings contribute at each offset. Because unshifted prediction already fails to help, these responses do not establish a coordination mechanism.",
