    {
      "name": "positive_completion",
      "caption": "Left: the original mean errors for all four laboratory folds, each with 32 held-out healthy participants. Both-leg correction is compared with own-leg correction, giving a 5.2% mean reduction across participants; linear interpolation is the added descriptive benchmark. Right: the same both-leg predictor is trained with Anatomical or Random masking and evaluated on identical GAVD targets. Anatomical training reduces grouped-hiding error by 7.7%; the scattered-hiding difference is uncertain. Error bars are the unchanged conditional paired 95% intervals. These are post-outcome descriptive completion comparisons, not improved anomaly-detection results.",
